nd such as with a  hundred years of excluding fire  the kinds of fires that are burning are  not the kinds that burned historically  and we want to get back to putting fire  in the ecosystem as a process but under  the natural range of variability that  you would have seen it not some of these  catastrophic wildfires that are a result  a direct result of huge fuel build ups  and droughty climates we're a global  school of the environment that  encompasses quite a broad arena we  define forestry much more broadly than  many schools do for more information  about the Yale School of Forestry and  environmental studies visit environment  yale edu
 

